A||N||2||grgoyl86||Adding a Third Brake Light to an 85?||||1||
Z||000000||grgoyl86||10-07-2001||07:13 PM||||I have a question for a friend. No, seriously.  8^)<P>Anyway, I know someone who is trying to add a thrid brake light to an 85 GT. He has the light in place, and the wire (factory wire removed from a later Fiero) run up to the dash. But, he says the connection is different (he had looked at an 87 to see where it connects).<P>So, has someone out there done this already? Is there a place to just plug it in? Does he need to splice it somewhere? If so, where?<P>Thanks!<P><P>------------------<BR>Why do we park in driveways and drive on parkways?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||10-07-2001||08:33 PM||||Easiest way is to tap into the brake switch on the pedal. No hassels with the blinker circuitry.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||10-07-2001||09:03 PM||||Phil is correct, that's exactly what I would do.<P>Your friend is also correct about the connection.  There is a cross car wiring harness that changes 2 important connectors in '86.  This harness also contains the dome lights, power windows, and power lock circuitry.  If you are looking to add power locks or windows, make sure you get the correct harness for your year because the addition of the third brake light changes those two connectors.||||reg||1
